.SH "NAME"
econf_newKeyFile_with_options \- create a new econf_file object with special options

.SH "SYNOPSIS"

.sp
.ft B
.nf
#include <libeconf\&.h>
.fi
.ft
.sp

.BI "econf_err econf_newKeyFile_with_options(econf_file\ **" "result" ", const\ char\ *" "options" ");"

.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.PP
The \fBeconf_newKeyFile_with_options\fR() function creates a new, empty \fBeconf_file\fR object and stores it in \fI*result\fR\&.

.PP
\fIoptions\fR is a string of \fB<key>=<value>\fR pairs separated by \*(Aq;\*(Aq, e\&.g\&. \fB"JOIN_SAME_ENTRIES=1"\fR\&. If \fIoptions\fR is \fBNULL\fR or an empty string, the new \fBeconf_file\fR object is created with the default settings described below\&.

.PP
The following options are supported:

.PP
\fBJOIN_SAME_ENTRIES\fR (default 0)
.RS 4
          Parsed entries with the same name will not be replaced but will be joined to one entry\&.

.RE

.PP
\fBPYTHON_STYLE\fR (default 0)
.RS 4
          Indentations will be handled like multiline entries\&.

.RE

.PP
\fBDEFAULT_QUOTES\fR (default 0)
.RS 4
          Entries which are newly created (e\&.g\&. via \fBeconf_setStringValue\fR()) and not read from a file will have their value enclosed by quotes when the \fBeconf_file\fR is written to a file\&. This default can be overridden per entry with \fBeconf_setQuotes\fR()\&.

.RE

.PP
\fBPARSING_DIRS\fR (default /usr/etc/:/run:/etc)
.RS 4
          List of directories from which the configuration files have to be parsed\&. The list is a string, divided by \*(Aq:\*(Aq\&. The last entry has the highest priority\&. E\&.g\&.: \fB"PARSING_DIRS=/usr/etc/:/run:/etc"\fR\&.

.RE

.PP
\fBCONFIG_DIRS\fR (default empty)
.RS 4
          List of directory structures (with order) which describes the directories in which the files have to be parsed\&. The list is a string, divided by \*(Aq:\*(Aq\&. The last entry has the highest priority\&. E\&.g\&. with the given list \fB"CONFIG_DIRS=.conf.d:.d"\fR
files in the following directories will be parsed:
.sp
.RS 4
<default_dirs>/<config_name>\&.conf\&.d/
.br
<default_dirs>/<config_name>\&.d/
.br
<default_dirs>/<config_name>/
.RE

.RE

.PP
\fBROOT_PREFIX\fR (default empty)
.RS 4
          Directory prefix used for all search directories if specified\&.

.RE

.SH "RETURN VALUE"

.PP
Upon successful completion, this function returns \fBECONF_SUCCESS\fR and stores the newly created \fBeconf_file\fR object in \fI*result\fR\&.

.PP
On error, a non\-zero error code is returned (see the section called \(lqERRORS\(rq), and \fI*result\fR may be set to \fBNULL\fR\&.

.SH "ERRORS"

.PP
\fBECONF_NOMEM\fR
.RS 4
          Insufficient memory to allocate the new \fBeconf_file\fR object or one of its internal lists\&.

.RE

.PP
\fBECONF_OPTION_NOT_FOUND\fR
.RS 4
          \fIoptions\fR contains a key that is not a known option\&.

.RE

.SH "EXAMPLES"

.PP
.nf
#include <libeconf\&.h>

econf_file *key_file = NULL;
econf_err error;

if ((error = econf_newKeyFile_with_options(&key_file, "PYTHON_STYLE=1")))
{
  fprintf (stderr, "ERROR: couldn\*(Aqt create new key file: %s\en",
           econf_errString(error));
  return 1;
}

error = econf_readConfig (&key_file,
                          "foo",
                          "/usr/lib",
                          "example",
                          "conf",
                          "=", "#");

econf_free (key_file);
key_file = NULL;
.fi

